+# v0 trained-at-four action-depth sweep
+
+**Goal:** Automatically evaluate the same full-LIBERO v0 4/4 checkpoint at action depths 1, 2, 3, 5, 6, in that order; NFE 10; 6,000 episodes each.
+
+**Architecture:** Isolated checkout of upstream 56e3328. Strictly load and validate the original checkpoint before enabling a bounded inference-only action-depth override. Reuse the unchanged Light-WAM rollout and native v0 cached inference, including existing late-clamped video KV mapping. Persistent worker processes, resumable atomic task/seed groups, and a serial queue preserve simulator RNG order.
+
+**Protocol:** Four standard LIBERO suites; ten tasks; seeds 42,43,44; states 0..49; 30 settling steps; caps 400/400/400/700; predict32/execute10; FP32 weights/BF16 compute; exact native action conversion. Video depth remains4. Original K4 result remains a historical reference, with a fresh K4 compatibility gate. No separately trained K1/K2 checkpoints.
+
+**Review focus:** Wrong checkpoint or depth; changes to video KV alignment; missing/duplicate resumed episodes; different rollout or RNG rules; speed changes that alter actions or outcomes.
+
+- [ ] Add failing tests for inference depth bounds, training rejection, unchanged K4 outputs and physical action-block/KV schedules.
+- [ ] Add minimal explicit inference-only override; run relevant tests and repository CPU suite.
+- [ ] Freeze checkpoint/assets/source/task identities and prior K4 provenance.
+- [ ] Build resumable runner and serial queue with strict condition identity and episode validation; test accounting and recovery.
+- [ ] Verify every requested depth on real simulator inputs, including K4 comparison against previous code. Test CUDA graphs per depth and select fastest validated worker profile under available VRAM.
+- [ ] Launch detached queue, verify a scored episode, and record progress, logs, and measured ETA in evaluation_report/v0_ka_sweep.
+
+Bulk outputs: /data14t/anhdh35/loopwam_v0_ka_sweep_20261027. Queue and runner: isolated checkout scripts/v0_ka_*.py. Model weights are never rewritten. Local pre-pull reports are backed up separately and restored.
